    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0365" n="257" xml:id="pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/437: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-04T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 4,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 4—5:24
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your February 3, 5 p.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d246-f1"/> I have not advised or
                    suggested withdrawal of Americans from Shanghai to Manila. I have advised quiet
                    withdrawal of women and children from the interior to Shanghai while lines of
                    communication in the district remain open and safe and have cautioned all
                    Americans to be prepared to withdraw without delay preferably to Shanghai or to
                    ports where they may be protected or if necessary evacuated. Gradual withdrawal
                    women and children to Shanghai is proceeding. The plans being worked out here in
                    cooperation with the Navy for the safety of Americans at Shanghai contemplate
                    that in the remote contingency that Shanghai should be attacked or any very
                    serious disorders occur threatening safety of Americans, the evacuation of
                    American women and children and, if necessary, men to Manila would be carried
                    out.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
